# A method with a callable formal (l2_cf_get) is outside the walkable subset (l2_rw_may) --
# --walk-methods now refuses it, located, instead of silently leaving it native
# (next_core_tasks.md §7 "Интерпретаторы: те же два примера или явное unsupported";
# steps/interpreters-callable-parity-t6t7.md). Without the knob this translates and runs fine
# (see unit_t7_convert.lm2's `take`, the fuller T7 witness); this row only exists to pin the
# --walk-methods refusal text with a minimal reproduction.
fn: bin () int
    return: 0

fn: take (bin: op) int
    return: op()

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: take(bin); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
